Package: axiom-firewall
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: The Axiom contributors <51213010+a-51-50@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/a-51-50/Axiom
Depends: @SHLIBS_DEPENDS@, nftables, polkitd | policykit-1, pkexec | policykit-1, systemd
Conflicts: axiom (<< 1000)
Replaces: axiom (<< 1000)
Recommends: linux-tools-common | bpftool, libsecret-1-0, gnome-shell-extension-appindicator | plasma-workspace
Description: Network and AI agent security (desktop app + axiomd service)
 Axiom is a free, open-source per-application firewall with connection
 monitoring, history, Privacy Shield DNS filtering and AI-agent awareness.
 .
 This package installs the desktop application under /usr/lib/axiom-firewall
 and a launcher in /usr/bin, plus the privileged background service axiomd as
 a systemd unit (root-owned image in /usr/libexec/axiom, data in
 /var/lib/axiom). Rules are enforced with nftables (socket cgroupv2) and, when
 bpftool and a BTF-enabled kernel are available, a connect-time eBPF layer.
